                  <handDesc>
                     <handNote xml:id="h1" script="Ethiopic">
                        <locus from="1r" to="84va"/>
                        <seg type="script">Nineteenth-century script.</seg> 
                        <seg type="ink">Black and red (deep reddish brown, <locus target="#55r"/>; vivid vermilion, e.g., <locus target="#35rb #41rb"/>).</seg>
                        <desc>Mediocre; the ligature <foreign xml:lang="gez">ግ</foreign>+<foreign xml:lang="gez">ዚ</foreign> in <foreign xml:lang="gez">እግዚአብሔር</foreign> and 
                           <foreign xml:lang="gez">እግዚእ</foreign> is used, but very inconsistently (cp. <locus target="#27v #47v"/>).
                           <persName role="scribe" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15263GabraMar">Gabra Mā<supplied reason="omitted" cert="medium">ryām</supplied></persName> (?) is mentioned as the scribe on <locus target="#84va"/>.</desc>
                        
                        <list type="abbreviations">
                           <item>
                              <abbr>ም፡, ምዕ፡</abbr> for <abbr>ምዕራፍ፡</abbr> 
                              <abbr>በእ፡</abbr> for <expan>በእንተ፡</expan> (<locus target="#84r #84v"/>)</item>
                        </list>
                        <seg type="rubrication">Divine names; a few lines (some in groups of two)
                           alternating with black lines on the opening page; numbers and headings of
                           the chapters; elements of the punctuation signs; elements of the numerals
                           and of the quire marks.</seg>
                     </handNote>
                  </handDesc>
